 "open_polygons": [],
 "notes": "Excelsior, Brazil Ave to below France Ave, London St to Dublin St: a regular grid of long blocks turned about 31 deg, with RH-1/RH-2 borders along Brazil and the avenue south of Persia, and P boxes on 6088 and 6075 (zoning borders over lines do not split blocks). 53 blocks, many cut by the box sides; no open land. Judgment calls: (1) Bottom edge near x 1250-1300, y 3191-3215: below block 6281 the avenue meets the McLaren Park land (6284A) and its line is hidden under the heavy P border; I typed the park corner with its west side on the thin line at (1262,3195)-(1250,3215) and its top on the line of the avenue's far side as in the block to the west, so the heavy border strip just below 6281 is labelled street. (2) Block 6284 (bottom right, x 1486-1564, y 3156-3215): its east side is a thin line not on the grid angle, (1564,3180) to (1554,3215), beside a heavy border; the land east of it inside the box is street. (3) Where a heavy border lies on an avenue line (Brazil Ave, the RH-1/RH-2 border avenue) the block side was set from the block's other ends and the neighbouring blocks on the same line.",
 "drawn_by": "Claude (AI), 2026-11-23: block sides measured from page.png ink, not typed by eye: the street grid here is a rectangle grid turned 31.1 deg (angle from line fits on the thin ink); in that turned frame each block's four sides were set at the outer edge of its thin line (median over many cross-sections, skipping spots under heavy ink or letters), corners turned back to page px and clipped to the box; three sides hidden under heavy zoning lines and one non-grid side (block 6284) set by hand from close-ups; every outline then checked by eye on 4x ruled close-ups and the labels picture"
